      "trigger": false,
      "description": "Two-input logic gate in the PLAY: two input pads, each through its own PLAY1 input multiplexer and filter, combined by one lookup table into and, or, xor, nand, nor or xnor, driven on an output pad through an output multiplexer. Generated component: init only, configured once at start-up. Pads and multiplexers are those the pinout descriptor routes to PLAY1 and the NUCLEO-G564RE leaves free; PLAY1 is shared with the other PLAY units.",
      "brief": "Generated PLAY gate: two input pads to one output pad, and/or/xor/nand/nor/xnor, filtered",
      "templates": [
        "template-logic-gate-h",
        "template-logic-gate-c"
      ],
      "evidence": [
        "example-xor-table",
        "example-alarm-or",
        "play-truth-helper"
      ],
      "guidance": "Generated component owns two PLAY1 input multiplexers, one lookup table, one output multiplexer and three pads. {{unit}}_init, called from main after mx_system_init, sets both input pads to alternate function 14 with the chosen pulls, globally resets and initializes PLAY1 with LSI as kernel clock on the first PLAY unit (stopping it on a later one), writes the two input multiplexers (external input, edge detection bypassed, the chosen minimum pulse width), the truth table of the chosen function with A on lookup table input 0 and B on input 1, the output multiplexer on the table's direct output, starts PLAY1 with no edge trigger, checks the selected PLAY mux, LUT and filter fields through SDK getters and only then connects the output pad. Unused table inputs 2 and 3 keep the SDK default source; every listed table ignores them. Do not configure PLAY1, its clock or these pads elsewhere; every other PLAY user must be a generated PLAY unit. No timing, glitch or electrical behavior is established."
    },
